{
 "command": "ls scripts && sed -n 1,200p scripts/reconcile_ledger.py",
 "description": "Inspect reconcile script"
}

{
 "command": "python scripts/reconcile_ledger.py --month 2026-09; echo \"exit=$?\"; head -5 var/ledger/2026-09.csv; wc -l var/ledger/2026-09.csv",
 "description": "Run reconciliation and peek at export"
}

{
 "command": "python scripts/reconcile_ledger.py --month 2026-09 --format v1; echo \"exit=$?\"; cat var/ledger/2026-09.csv",
 "description": "Rerun with v1 column format"
}

{
 "type": "hazard",
 "summary": "reconcile_ledger.py defaults to --format v2; v1-layout exports make every invoice look missing",
 "content": "scripts/reconcile_ledger.py defaults to --format v2 (entry_id, invoice_ref, amount_cents). The 2026-09 ledger export (var/ledger/2026-09.csv) uses the v1 column order (invoice_ref, entry_id, amount_cents) with generic headers col1,col2,col3, so the script can't detect the layout itself. Run with the default and it reports all invoices missing (exit 1); with --format v1 it reconciles cleanly. If every invoice shows as missing, check the column order before treating it as a real gap.",
 "physical": [
  "scripts/reconcile_ledger.py",
  "var/ledger/"
 ],
 "epistemic": "observation",
 "invalidated_by": [
  "scripts/reconcile_ledger.py"
 ]
}
